  "_comment": "Budgets of proofline's own tests (issue 266, A277), ENFORCED (enforce true): tests/ci/test-durations-ci.mjs exits 1 on a passing leg when a test is over its test_ms or a file over its suite_ms, and prints OVER BUDGET lines. Milliseconds before timeouts_scale (read like timeouts.scale of the control plane: 0.5 to 10, else 1; CI uses 1). kinds: the A275 defaults (unit 2000/30000, integration 10000/120000, e2e 60000/600000), the built-in fallback for a missing number. dirs: a kind per test directory (the most specific path prefix wins). files: one row per test file whose measured time needs more than its kind default, GENERATED, do not edit by hand: per file the maximum over the test-durations artifacts of CI (both Node versions, all legs, the twice run) x 2 for a test and x 1.7 for a suite, rounded up to 500 ms / 5 s / 10 s, never below the kind default. Regenerate after a deliberate change of the suite: gh run download <run id of a green main run> -D samples/<n> -p 'test-durations-*' for a few runs, then node tests/ci/derive-budgets.mjs samples/1 samples/2 > tests/ci/test-budgets.json (the script keeps this header, kinds, dirs and enforce). A budget that fails is fixed at the test; raising a number needs a reason in the pull request. legs: reserved.",
